WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.334 --> 00:00:05.919
For the past five years,

00:00:05.961 --> 00:00:08.838
I've been working
as a psychologist in Russia,

00:00:08.880 --> 00:00:11.758
a country where mental
health is stigmatized

00:00:11.800 --> 00:00:14.761
and people are often afraid
to seek professional help.

00:00:15.387 --> 00:00:18.974
Right now, people in Ukraine
are fighting for their lives.

00:00:19.558 --> 00:00:22.852
What is happening
is devastating and traumatic,

00:00:22.894 --> 00:00:27.023
and everyone, including both
Russians and Ukrainians,

00:00:27.023 --> 00:00:30.360
will need mental health support,
but on different levels.

00:00:30.402 --> 00:00:33.238
No matter where in the world
I'll be working from,

00:00:33.280 --> 00:00:35.282
I'm committed to helping people.

00:00:35.865 --> 00:00:37.242
Psychotherapy for me,

00:00:37.284 --> 00:00:41.162
has and will always be
a force of understanding,

00:00:41.204 --> 00:00:42.956
change and peace.

00:00:42.956 --> 00:00:45.584
And now it is needed more than ever.

00:00:45.625 --> 00:00:50.046
Unfortunately, there is a lot
of resistance to psychotherapy in Russia.

00:00:50.046 --> 00:00:52.299
First, for historical reasons.

00:00:52.716 --> 00:00:54.134
During the Soviet Union,

00:00:54.175 --> 00:00:57.596
psychiatry was often used
as a political tool,

00:00:57.637 --> 00:01:01.641
and this is just a small part
of the state attitudes toward people

00:01:01.683 --> 00:01:04.019
that deeply traumatized the society.

00:01:04.436 --> 00:01:05.895
Since then,

00:01:05.895 --> 00:01:09.399
Russia has seen major reforms
in the psychiatric system,

00:01:09.441 --> 00:01:13.361
and there are a growing number of good
specialists in the mental health industry.

00:01:13.737 --> 00:01:15.655
Yet problems remain.

00:01:16.114 --> 00:01:20.118
As in many countries where mental
health has been stigmatized,

00:01:20.160 --> 00:01:23.830
proper regulations
for practicing psychologists

00:01:23.872 --> 00:01:26.124
have never been developed in Russia.

00:01:26.166 --> 00:01:28.960
There are no licensing procedures

00:01:29.002 --> 00:01:32.881
or any laws protecting clients
from incompetence and fraud.

00:01:33.423 --> 00:01:34.924
There are a lot of scammers,

00:01:34.966 --> 00:01:37.385
people who simply took
a three-month course,

00:01:37.427 --> 00:01:39.971
tarot card readers or astrologers

00:01:39.971 --> 00:01:42.432
who say they're
professional psychologists.

00:01:42.807 --> 00:01:44.017
As a result,

00:01:44.017 --> 00:01:47.103
a lot of people don't know
how to choose a professional

00:01:47.145 --> 00:01:48.730
who fits their profile

00:01:48.730 --> 00:01:52.192
or are even victimized
by such unprofessional help.

00:01:52.942 --> 00:01:56.738
In the absence of regulation
and interest by the state,

00:01:56.780 --> 00:01:58.490
I saw an opportunity.

00:01:58.990 --> 00:02:01.284
With my team, we created a platform

00:02:01.326 --> 00:02:03.953
with an assessment system
for psychologists

00:02:03.953 --> 00:02:08.041
and the means to get people connected
to the therapists they need,

00:02:08.083 --> 00:02:10.085
therapists they can trust.

00:02:10.627 --> 00:02:12.128
Through this assessment system,

00:02:12.128 --> 00:02:17.050
we help people overcome the risk
of being harmed by professional help

00:02:17.092 --> 00:02:19.052
or falling into despair,

00:02:19.094 --> 00:02:22.097
of giving up hope
they will ever feel better.

00:02:23.056 --> 00:02:28.019
We have based our assessment
on a hypothesis backed up with research,

00:02:28.061 --> 00:02:30.438
saying that there are common factors

00:02:30.480 --> 00:02:34.317
that significantly contribute
to psychotherapy effectiveness.

00:02:34.859 --> 00:02:37.529
This includes a variety of ways

00:02:37.529 --> 00:02:39.864
in which a therapist and the client

00:02:39.864 --> 00:02:43.201
create a special bond
of trust and partnership.

00:02:43.243 --> 00:02:47.706
Unfortunately, in most psychotherapy
training programs in Russia,

00:02:47.747 --> 00:02:51.292
not much attention is paid
to those common factors.

00:02:52.001 --> 00:02:54.045
The bottom line,

00:02:54.087 --> 00:02:56.589
having a good diploma is not enough.

00:02:57.257 --> 00:03:01.720
Our psychologists undergo a test
and a case study interview,

00:03:01.761 --> 00:03:03.596
including ethics questions,

00:03:03.638 --> 00:03:06.599
because the client's safety
is the priority.

00:03:06.975 --> 00:03:11.146
The sad truth is that only around
15 percent of applicants

00:03:11.146 --> 00:03:13.690
pass our selective assessment screening.

00:03:14.065 --> 00:03:15.567
After this assessment,

00:03:15.608 --> 00:03:19.821
it is important to match a client
with the right specialist.

00:03:19.863 --> 00:03:21.740
With our current matching algorithm,

00:03:21.740 --> 00:03:25.535
we've already helped
more than 35,000 people

00:03:25.577 --> 00:03:27.620
receive safe psychotherapy.

00:03:28.288 --> 00:03:31.040
We also offer pro-bono sessions

00:03:31.082 --> 00:03:32.876
and free educational materials

00:03:32.917 --> 00:03:35.712
to support those who can't afford therapy.

00:03:36.212 --> 00:03:41.843
And I believe the number of people
in need of mental health support

00:03:41.843 --> 00:03:44.596
will increase due to the PTSD,

00:03:44.596 --> 00:03:45.805
chronic stress,

00:03:45.847 --> 00:03:49.058
trauma of two years of the pandemic

00:03:49.100 --> 00:03:52.187
and all the global events
we are experiencing.

00:03:52.937 --> 00:03:54.314
And this is the beginning

00:03:54.355 --> 00:03:58.401
of a bigger mental health catastrophe
we all need to face.

00:03:58.943 --> 00:04:00.403
We're trying our best,

00:04:00.445 --> 00:04:03.364
even though we work in a tough environment

00:04:03.364 --> 00:04:04.824
with the strong stigma

00:04:04.866 --> 00:04:08.912
and the cultural memory of psychiatry
as an instrument of oppression.

00:04:09.496 --> 00:04:14.751
Our goal is to minimize the risk
of people giving up on therapy

00:04:14.793 --> 00:04:16.336
because it's dangerous.

00:04:16.377 --> 00:04:17.962
On an individual level,

00:04:18.004 --> 00:04:22.008
it means a barrier for well-being,
and unfolding potential.

00:04:22.050 --> 00:04:23.343
For the world,

00:04:23.384 --> 00:04:26.721
it means a loss
in productivity and economy.

00:04:27.222 --> 00:04:29.724
Just depression and anxiety disorder

00:04:29.724 --> 00:04:33.978
cause the global economy an estimated
one trillion dollars each year

00:04:34.020 --> 00:04:35.772
in lost productivity.

00:04:36.231 --> 00:04:39.567
But I believe that the most
important costs

00:04:39.609 --> 00:04:43.238
are the decrease in the quality
of connections between people.

00:04:43.571 --> 00:04:45.824
The loss of self awareness.

00:04:46.157 --> 00:04:49.118
An increase in hatred and violence.

00:04:50.245 --> 00:04:54.374
Psychotherapy is not only
about one individual finding help

00:04:54.374 --> 00:04:56.584
for their individual issues.

00:04:58.169 --> 00:05:02.298
When one of us is wounded,
all of us share in that wound.

00:05:03.049 --> 00:05:07.971
Psychotherapy is a way to move forward
from the burden of the past

00:05:08.012 --> 00:05:09.931
and trauma of the present

00:05:09.931 --> 00:05:12.100
by breaking cycles of hurt,

00:05:12.141 --> 00:05:16.312
by embracing the path of healing
and self-knowledge.

00:05:16.771 --> 00:05:22.318
Because by knowing ourselves and seeking
healing from our pain and trauma,

00:05:22.360 --> 00:05:27.365
we also become better human beings
in our interconnected world,

00:05:27.407 --> 00:05:31.369
bringing a real hope for peace.

00:05:31.870 --> 00:05:33.037
Thank you.

00:05:33.037 --> 00:05:36.791
(Applause)

